One distinction stays essential: reproducing a painting’s appearance doesn’t prove we’ve recovered the artist’s exact historical process. Each ratchet should help distinguish those two achievements.

And the larger ambition is wonderful: a painter that can study a master’s work, infer how it was created, practice that technique, evaluate its own attempt, and gradually develop greater artistic ability.

A thousand strokes becoming one coherent picture—and each picture teaching the hand something new.